'''Kelvin Ridge''' was a location on the [[planet]] [[Jakku]].

==History==
After the [[First Order]] [[Attack on Tuanul|attack]] on [[Tuanul]], the [[droid]] [[BB-8]] fled, eventually running into the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] who convinced a local [[Teedo (Niima Outpost)|Teedo]] to leave the droid alone. Rey then pointed BB-8 in the direction of [[Niima Outpost]] but warned him to stay off Kelvin Ridge.<ref name="TFA novel" />

==Behind the scenes==
Kelvin Ridge is named after [[J.J. Abrams]]'s grandfather, whose first name was Kelvin. The director has used the name Kelvin in many of his projects: It appears as the name of a ship in ''Star Trek'', as the intended recipient of a postcard intercepted by Tom Cruise in ''Mission: Impossible III'', as the name of a chain of gas stations in ''Super 8'', as the name of a characters on ''Alias'' and ''Lost'' and as the name of a business on ''Fringe''.<ref>{{WebCite|url=https://screencrush.com/star-wars-abrams-easter-egg|text='Star Wars: The Force Awakens' Features J.J. Abrams' Signature Easter Egg|author=Hayes, Britt|date=2015-12-19|archivedate=20200504113745}}</ref>

